. 2013;8:e81884.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0081884</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC3846781</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">24312598</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Baviera&#x2010;Mu&#xf1;oz R, Carretero&#x2010;Vilarroig L, Pedro&#x2010;Ibor A, Jaijo T, Del Valle&#x2010;Carranza A, Mart&#xed;nez&#x2010;Torres I, et al. <i>STUB1</i> mutations as possible genetic modifiers in spinocerebellar ataxia type 8. Mov Disord. 2024;mds.29910.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">38962894</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Magri S, Nanetti L, Gellera C, Sarto E, Rizzo E, Mongelli A, et al. Digenic inheritance of <i>STUB1</i> variants and <i>TBP</i> polyglutamine expansions explains the incomplete penetrance of SCA17 and SCA48. Genet Med. 2022;24:29&#x2013;40.
